    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented email-uniqueness enforcement on `POST /api/owners`, mirroring the existing telephone-uniqueness check. When a create request supplies an email whose lower-cased form already belongs to another owner, the endpoint now responds **409 Conflict**.\n\nFiles added:\n- `rest/function/owner/CheckEmailUnique.java` \u2014 a pipeline step that reads the validated body (email already lower-cased by `ValidateOwner`), skips when email is absent/blank (email is optional), and throws `DuplicateEmailException` if any existing owner's lower-cased email matches.\n- `rest/escalation/DuplicateEmailException.java` \u2014 checked exception carrying the offending email.\n- `rest/escalation/DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `409` with body `{\"errors\":[\"email\"]}`.\n- `officefloor/escalation/...DuplicateEmailException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\nFile changed:\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `checkEmail` step (governed by `transaction`) between `checkTelephone` and `checkHousehold`.\n\nThe new `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` acceptance test and the rest of the suite pass.",
